  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x74" flags="0x0">
    <title>B1 - Supercharger upper pressure ratio diagnosis threshold</title>
    <description>Maximum modeled supercharger pressure ratio versus engine speed. A sustained excess confirmed by diagnosis selects the bypass fallback position. Evidence: CPU CB406..CB444: interpolate pointer834F (DPP2=23 -&gt; fileC34F), compare E2D6 &gt; (lookup &lt;&lt;8), qualify through D30D0 and latch FD30.6. CB4A0..CB4A4 combines FD30.5/6 into FD30.4; E32FA..E3330 selects fallback cal971E. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 230kompressor_EVO_Joao.bin. Calibration block 1. Monitor enabled with FD12.8 set and FD2A.5, FD52.9, FD30.4 and FD22.12 clear. Ratio = raw/64, not bar or gauge boost. The upper monitor uses modeled E2D6, approximately 16384*E2BE/E2C8, rather than direct measured MAP/ambient pressure. Diagnostic qualification time in seconds, complete latch-reset conditions and exact DTC mapping are not established.</description>
