  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x81" flags="0x0">
    <title>B2 - Bypass actuator position feedforward curve</title>
    <description>Position-dependent feedforward added to motor feedback terms. Evidence: CPU E27DC..E2888 selects axis and curve using BC002/BC1F2, subtracts0x8000; sums terms. E288C..E2928 limits and outputs PW3. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 230kompressor_EVO_Joao.bin. Calibration block 2. Second motorized air flap: actual E3A2, target E3C4, motor PW3; distinct from main throttle E5EA/PW2. Bypass/recirculation identification is strongly supported by the air-path calculation and two-actuator architecture, but no verified physical connector-to-RAM or manufacturer symbol has been recovered. Position values remain native sensor counts, not degrees or percent. Actuator-control calibration, not a requested boost or flap-position map. Motor command units are native, centered raw32768.</description>
