    <description>Upper engine speed cap. The lowest enabled cap becomes the active limit. Evidence: CPU DCACA..DCB8D takes the minimum of enabled byte caps; DCB82..DCB86 shifts left 5 and stores active limit E36A. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 230kompressor_EVO_Joao.bin. Calibration block 2. FD2C.3=1 and FD08.3=1 and D06F &gt; cal9344. State flags are named by their exact RAM bit. Manual/automatic, neutral and clutch labels are not proven for FD2C.3/FD78.5/E040/E041. D06F has not been identified; it must not be confused with coolant byte E06F.</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>Index</units>
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
