  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xe7" flags="0x0">
    <title>B2 - Protection RPM limit - FD8A.13</title>
    <description>Upper engine speed cap. The lowest enabled cap becomes the active limit. Evidence: CPU DCACA..DCB8D takes the minimum of enabled byte caps; DCB82..DCB86 shifts left 5 and stores active limit E36A. Confidence: structure transferred from M10062; target program unavailable Source image: 230kompressor_EVO_Joao.bin. Calibration block 2. FD8A.13=1. State flags are named by their exact RAM bit. Manual/automatic, neutral and clutch labels are not proven for FD2C.3/FD78.5/E040/E041.</description>
